            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery fistula into a persistent left superior vena cava: report of a case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>966-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We herein report the rare case of a patient with coronary artery fistula (CAF) between the left circumflex coronary artery and persistent left superior vena cava (PLSVC) with a complete absence of the right superior vena cava (SVC).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
